Used, not included
------------------

ffmpeg and ffprobe (https://ffmpeg.org) encode media. Elabora runs the copy it finds through
ELABORA_FFMPEG / ELABORA_FFPROBE or on the PATH, as a separate program. The continuous
integration uses the GPL builds of BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds. ffmpeg is licensed under the LGPL 2.1
or later, and its GPL builds under the GPL 2 or later.

Pocket TTS (https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts, CC-BY 4.0) and the speech models for word
alignment and transcription are downloaded on first use. Their credits are recorded with the
audio they make.

npm dependencies keep their own licences (mostly MIT, ISC, BSD and Apache-2.0). Optional ones:
scorm-again (MIT) and playwright-core (Apache-2.0) for the LMS emulator, axe-core (MPL-2.0) for
accessibility checks, onnxruntime-node (MIT) for local voices. Of all these dependencies, course packages ship D3 (ISC) alone: it is
bundled, with its notice, into a free object that imports it.
